# PR Review Prevention — Ship It Right The First Time

Each rule below exists because a real core-fe PR shipped without it and a human
reviewer had to catch it. Treat them as part of "done", not as review feedback.

Procedures: `agent-os/skills/guard-authoring/SKILL.md` (gates) ·
`agent-os/skills/pre-pr-sweep/SKILL.md` (the full sweep).

## A gate you have not watched fail is not a gate

Adding a validator, an eslint restriction, or a CI step is **not** evidence it
works. Before claiming a gate is landed:

1. Create a synthetic violation and confirm the gate **flags** it.
2. Confirm the exempt/allowed case still **passes**.
3. Probe from every layer glob that can reach the violation — ESLint flat config
   **replaces** rule options rather than merging them, so a restriction added to
   one block is inert for files matched by a later block.
4. Wire it into `.github/workflows/pr-ci.yml`. `health-check.sh` is local-only;
   a locally-skippable invariant is an unenforced one.

## Never read an exit code through a pipe

`pnpm lint | tail -5` reports `tail`'s status. Capture the real one
(`cmd > file 2>&1; echo $?`) or `set -o pipefail`. Reporting a gate as green on a
piped command has already produced a false "all passing" on this repo.

## Finish the sweep or scope it to whole units

When applying a pattern across the codebase, do not stop at the list you started
with — grep for sibling forms (`aria-label` → `title` → `placeholder`) and for
remaining instances. If the sweep cannot be finished, convert **whole components**
and declare the boundary in the PR body. A half-converted component is a bug; an
untouched one is a known gap.

## Deleting a surface means deleting its registrations

Route mounts, service-worker precache patterns, vendor chunk lists, analytics
events, store slices, locale keys, constants, test ids, and docs. `knip` does not
see orphaned locale keys, and a constant referenced only by its own test is dead —
a test is not a consumer.

## A staleness guard must cover every path

Extract it into a helper and route all call sites through it; grep the protected
mutation to confirm. Guards belong at the mutation boundary, not in the caller —
the caller cannot protect side effects that happen behind an `await`.

## Module-scope `import()` defeats code splitting

Top-level dynamic imports execute at module evaluation. Use `onceAsync()`
(`src/lib/lazy-module.ts`) for a shared module promise without the eager fetch.
`pnpm build:check` will not catch this — it tripwires the static preload graph.

## Regenerate derived artifacts last

`pnpm sync:check` (project tree, TSDoc budget, locale parity) runs **after** the
final file is added, and again after any new file. Running it mid-change is how a
stale `project-tree.txt` reaches CI.

## Keep the PR body true to the branch

Before requesting review, reconcile the description against
`git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD`. Fix stale counts, claims a later commit
reversed, and workstreams added since it was written. Do not overclaim in the
title — scope the wording to what actually shipped.
